        "original_id": "44221ed7-a582-53a5-98a0-d3beb1826eb2",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Michael Jackson, Bob Giraldi, Quincy Jones\n- Works: “Beat It”, Thriller, E.T. the Extra-Terrestrial, “Dinner Rush”\n- Organizations: Westlake Recording Studios, MCA Records\n- Places: Los Angeles\n\nFacts:\n- Bob Giraldi was born on January 17, 1939.\n- Thriller is Michael Jackson’s sixth solo album and was released in 1982.\n- “Beat It” is a song written and performed by American singer Michael Jackson, and it was released as a single from Thriller.\n- Recording sessions for Thriller took place from April to November 1982 at Westlake Recording Studios in Los Angeles, with a production budget of $750,000.\n- Bob Giraldi is an American film and television director known for directing Dinner Rush and the music video for Michael Jackson’s “Beat It.”\n- E.T. the Extra-Terrestrial was narrated by Michael Jackson, produced by Quincy Jones, and distributed by MCA Records.",
